Summary:Chinese investors are buying up Western video game companies to gain access to the lucrative Chinese market, which is growing at 15% a year and worth $24.4bn in 2016.
, slice_answer: Chinese investors are buying up Western video game companies to gain access to the lucrative Chinese market, which is growing at 15% a year and worth $24.4bn in 2016.
